<div id="2026-09-25-ai-eval-reports" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-25 — Daily AI Eval Reports on /ai/eval (review-first proposals, allow-listed apply)</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> The AI usage monitor's daily eval report now lives in the app. New Results <code>AiEvalReport</code> (table <code>ai_eval_report</code>, unique report_date + source) and <code>AiEvalProposal</code> (<code>ai_eval_proposal</code>), both pending schema-compare. <code>Model::AI2::EvalReports</code> handles ingest (upsert, proposal dedupe by title), review, approve / reject, apply / revert. Admin-only pages <code>/ai/eval</code> and <code>/ai/eval/report/&lt;id&gt;</code> use plain POST forms with a CSRF token. A summary card sits on <code>/ai/usage</code>. <code>POST /ai/eval/ingest</code> needs a Bearer token (<code>AI_EVAL_INGEST_TOKEN</code> or <code>~/.comserv/secrets/ai_eval_ingest_token</code>) or an admin session. There is also an inbox import from <code>data/ai_eval_inbox/*.json</code>; today's report is seeded there.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> Admins should be able to review and tune the daily results, and the aisystem should improve only through changes a human approved. Nothing auto-applies. Apply works only on approved <code>config</code> proposals whose target is in <code>Util/AI/EvalAllowList.pm</code>. Each apply is atomic, logged and revertible. Code / workstation proposals become todos in project AISYSTEM.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/AI/Eval.pm</code> <code>Model/AI2/EvalReports.pm</code> <code>Util/AI/EvalAllowList.pm</code> <code>Result/{AiEvalReport,AiEvalProposal}.pm</code> <code>Model/Schema/Ency.pm</code> <code>Controller/AI.pm</code> (usage card) <code>Util/AI/Glossary.{pm,md}</code> <code>root/ai/eval/*.tt</code> <code>root/ai/usage_eval_card.tt</code> <code>root/ai/usage.tt</code> <code>data/ai_eval_inbox/2026-09-25-ai-usage-monitor.json</code> <code>script/ai_eval_ingest.pl</code> <code>t/ai_eval_reports.t</code></p>
</div>
